    {"role": "assistant", "text": "Data platform monitoring spans infrastructure, data quality, and business metrics. Missing any layer means you'll miss critical failures. Here's the complete stack:\n\n**Infrastructure Monitoring (Prometheus + Grafana):**\n\n```yaml\n# Key Prometheus metrics to scrape\nkafka_metrics:\n  - kafka_consumer_lag_records_lag  # Consumer falling behind = backpressure\n  - kafka_server_bytes_in_per_sec   # Throughput monitoring\n  - kafka_log_size_bytes            # Disk usage\n  \nflink_metrics:\n  - flink_taskmanager_job_task_operator_numRecordsIn  # Processing rate\n  - flink_jobmanager_job_numberOfFailedCheckpoints    # Checkpoint health\n  - flink_taskmanager_Status_JVM_Memory_Heap_Used    # Memory pressure\n\nclickhouse_metrics:\n  - clickhouse_metrics_query_active    # Active queries\n  - clickhouse_metrics_memory_tracked  # Memory usage\n  - clickhouse_profile_events_inserted_rows  # Write throughput\n\niceberg_metrics:\n  - iceberg_commit_duration          # How long writes take\n  - iceberg_scan_planning_duration   # Query planning overhead\n```\n\n**Data SLA monitoring (custom Airflow sensors):**\n\n```python\nclass DataFreshnessAlert(BaseOperator):\n    \"\"\"Alert if data is older than expected.\"\"\"\n    def execute(self, context):\n        latest = spark.sql(\"\"\"\n            SELECT MAX(event_time_utc) as latest_event\n            FROM iceberg.transactions\n        \"\"\").first()['latest_event']\n        \n        lag = datetime.utcnow() - latest\n        \n        if lag > timedelta(minutes=15):\n            notify_pagerduty(f'DATA FRESHNESS ALERT: transactions data is {lag.seconds//60}min stale')\n            raise AirflowException(f'Data freshness SLA violated: {lag}')\n\n# In your DAG: check every 5 minutes that data is fresh\nfreshness_check = DataFreshnessAlert(task_id='check_freshness', dag=dag)\n```\n\n**End-to-end pipeline health dashboard:**\n\nKey KPIs to display on a real-time ops dashboard:\n- Events/second arriving in Kafka (should be ~23K ± 20%)\n- Flink consumer lag (should be < 10 seconds)\n- Iceberg commits per hour (should match checkpoint frequency)\n- ClickHouse query p99 latency (should be < 500ms)\n- Data quality check pass rate (should be 100%)\n- Reconciliation discrepancy (should be < 0.01%)\n\n**Runbook for the most common failures:**\n\n```\nIncident: Kafka consumer lag spiking\n  P1 check: Is Flink cluster up? Check flink_taskmanager_count\n  P2 check: Is ingestion rate spiking? Check bytes_in_per_sec\n  P3 check: Did schema change break deserialization? Check DLQ size\n  Resolution: Scale Flink TaskManagers or fix serialization\n\nIncident: ClickHouse queries slow\n  P1 check: Is disk I/O maxed? Check disk_read_throughput\n  P2 check: Are too many concurrent queries? Check query_active\n  P3 check: Is a specific query hogging resources? Check query_log\n  Resolution: Kill expensive query, add to slow query blocklist\n```\n\n**Cost alerting (often forgotten):**\n```python\n# Daily cost budget alert\ndef check_daily_spend():\n    today_cost = cost_explorer.get_cost()\n    daily_budget = 2000  # $2K/day budget\n    if today_cost > daily_budget * 1.2:\n        alert(f'Cost overrun: ${today_cost:.0f} today (budget ${daily_budget})')\n```\n\nSet cost anomaly detection in AWS Cost Explorer — it will email you if costs are 20%+ above expected. This has saved data teams from surprise $100K bills from runaway Spark jobs.", "index": 41},
